1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,850
Grab a tape measure.

2
00:00:01,930 --> 00:00:03,510
In the next three minutes,

3
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:05,630
you'll know exactly what your body level

4
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:06,240
is.

5
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:08,620
Most guys train chest and abs all

6
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:10,840
year, and still look like a rectangle

7
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:11,820
in a t-shirt.

8
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:12,710
Hey.

9
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:14,890
Rectangles are a valid shape.

10
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:16,440
It's not your chest.

11
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:18,840
It's two muscles almost nobody trains at

12
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:19,520
home.

13
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:20,730
Stay to the end,

14
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:22,330
and you'll get the exact plan to

15
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:23,480
move up a level.

16
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:24,750
Here's the test.

17
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:27,000
Measure around your shoulders at the widest

18
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,700
point.

19
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:29,400
Then measure your waist at your belly

20
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:30,080
button.

21
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,730
Divide shoulders by waist.

22
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:34,510
That number is your level.

23
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:35,660
Level one.

24
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:37,250
Under one point two.

25
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:39,580
Shoulders and waist almost the same.

26
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:40,930
From the front, you look like a

27
00:00:40,930 --> 00:00:41,740
box.

28
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:43,480
Level two.

29
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,690
One point two to one point three.

30
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:47,200
There's a hint of a V,

31
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:49,080
but only when you stand up straight.

32
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:50,860
Level three.

33
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:53,060
One point three to one point four.

34
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:55,040
A clear V in a t-shirt.

35
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:56,660
This is where most people who train

36
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:58,160
for a year end up.

37
00:00:58,860 --> 00:00:59,920
Level four.

38
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,120
One point four to one point five.

39
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,370
Wide shoulders, narrow waist.

40
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:05,950
People ask if you swim.

41
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:07,730
Level five.

42
00:01:07,810 --> 00:01:09,120
Around one point six.

43
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:10,870
The comic book shape.

44
00:01:10,950 --> 00:01:12,540
Rare, but you can get close at

45
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:13,200
home.

46
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:14,870
I measured.

47
00:01:14,870 --> 00:01:16,950
I'm a level one point one.

48
00:01:17,001 --> 00:01:18,531
Then you have the most room to

49
00:01:18,531 --> 00:01:19,211
grow.

50
00:01:20,361 --> 00:01:22,881
Here's why most people get stuck.

51
00:01:22,961 --> 00:01:25,691
A V-taper is made of three things:

52
00:01:25,721 --> 00:01:28,011
wide shoulders, a wide back,

53
00:01:28,011 --> 00:01:29,521
and a narrow waist.

54
00:01:29,621 --> 00:01:31,641
Push-ups build the front of your shoulders

55
00:01:31,641 --> 00:01:32,731
and your chest.

56
00:01:32,811 --> 00:01:34,501
But the width comes from the side

57
00:01:34,501 --> 00:01:36,261
of your shoulders, and from your lats,

58
00:01:36,261 --> 00:01:37,961
the wings on your back.

59
00:01:38,061 --> 00:01:40,311
And belly fat widens your waist,

60
00:01:40,311 --> 00:01:41,921
so it pulls your number down from

61
00:01:41,921 --> 00:01:43,011
the other side.

62
00:01:43,111 --> 00:01:44,491
So here's the plan.

63
00:01:44,571 --> 00:01:45,591
Three days a week,

64
00:01:45,591 --> 00:01:46,521
at home.

65
00:01:47,221 --> 00:01:47,921
One.

66
00:01:48,001 --> 00:01:49,211
Pike push-ups.

67
00:01:49,291 --> 00:01:52,011
Hips high, head down between your hands.

68
00:01:52,091 --> 00:01:53,981
They hit your shoulders from above.

69
00:01:54,061 --> 00:01:55,681
Three sets of eight.

70
00:01:56,381 --> 00:01:57,031
Two.

71
00:01:57,111 --> 00:01:59,221
Side raises with two water bottles or

72
00:01:59,221 --> 00:02:00,181
a backpack.

73
00:02:00,261 --> 00:02:02,381
Slow, up to shoulder height.

74
00:02:02,461 --> 00:02:04,161
Three sets of fifteen.

75
00:02:04,241 --> 00:02:05,881
This is the move that makes you

76
00:02:05,881 --> 00:02:06,631
wider.

77
00:02:07,331 --> 00:02:08,051
Three.

78
00:02:08,131 --> 00:02:09,891
Rows under a sturdy table,

79
00:02:09,891 --> 00:02:11,841
or a towel around a door handle.

80
00:02:11,921 --> 00:02:13,431
Pull your elbows back.

81
00:02:13,511 --> 00:02:15,061
Three sets of ten.

82
00:02:15,141 --> 00:02:16,891
This builds your wings.

83
00:02:17,591 --> 00:02:18,711
And for the waist,

84
00:02:18,711 --> 00:02:20,591
walk every day and keep your protein

85
00:02:20,591 --> 00:02:21,221
high.

86
00:02:21,301 --> 00:02:23,391
A smaller waist raises your number just

87
00:02:23,391 --> 00:02:25,021
as much as bigger shoulders.

88
00:02:25,121 --> 00:02:27,061
Measure again in eight weeks.

89
00:02:27,141 --> 00:02:29,171
Moving up even one level changes how

90
00:02:29,171 --> 00:02:30,661
every shirt fits.

91
00:02:31,361 --> 00:02:32,821
What's your number right now?

92
00:02:32,901 --> 00:02:34,681
Comment your level, and be honest.
